+/// Set how far each of this body's shapes may move past its bounds before the broad phase moves its proxy (the
+/// margin of its fat AABB), in meters. Zero, the default, leaves each shape its own: an eighth of its extent, at most
+/// B3_MAX_AABB_MARGIN. A fast body made of many small shapes leaves every shape's bounds every step, and each proxy
+/// moved queries the trees again; a wider margin moves them seldom, at the cost of pairs found sooner. A shape's fat
+/// AABB takes the new margin the next time the shape leaves it.
+B3_API void b3Body_SetAabbMargin( b3BodyId bodyId, float margin );
+
+/// The fat AABB margin this body gives its shapes, or zero for each shape's own.
+B3_API float b3Body_GetAabbMargin( b3BodyId bodyId );
+
 /// Allow this body to rotate fast. Useful for axially symmetric bodies, such as vehicle wheels.
 /// Normally rotation speed is clamped to improve CCD. However, this clamping is unnecessary for
 /// bodies that only rotate fast around an axis of symmetry.
